# Default GTK3/GTK4 theme selection for new users (the light variant, matching the
# light default used by the sibling Kvantum and colour-scheme skel files). Installed
# to /etc/skel/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini by the kuura-shell package's package()
# (docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md), which replaces "@NAME@" with $DISTRO_NAME first -- this
# file cannot be static data like kwinrc, the active theme's name is only known at
# package-build time.
#
# gtk-theme-name selects this project's own theme, which ships ONE directory holding
# both variants (/usr/share/themes/<name>/gtk-4.0/{gtk.css,gtk-dark.css} -- GTK's own
# long-standing convention, see PKGBUILD's package() comment for the install layout).
# gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme is GTK's documented switch between the two;
# false here matches the light default.
#
# CAVEAT -- read before assuming this is proven end-to-end, report this rather than
# silently trusting it: these keys are the standard, documented GTK mechanism, not an
# invented one, but could NOT be confirmed changing a real app's appearance live in
# the guest image. GTK4 and libadwaita are not part of the metapackage's dependency
# graph (nothing in this repository currently installs them) and the guest has no
# network (`-nic none`, harness/spike/vm_capture.py) to add a GTK4 test app for the
# investigation. A live A/B test WAS possible with GTK3 instead (already present via
# firefox, a dependency of the test image): a throwaway theme with an unmistakable
# gtk.css vs. gtk-dark.css colour difference was installed and selected through
# exactly this gtk-3.0/settings.ini mechanism (gtk-theme-name + prefer-dark-theme),
# then Firefox was launched fresh -- no visible change of any kind, even though the
# portal-based mechanism (docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md's "Dark mode" section) demonstrably
# DOES change live in the same image. The most likely explanation is that Firefox's
# own chrome does not render through the system GTK theme's CSS at all (a known
# Firefox/GTK quirk, not necessarily evidence that the gtk.css/gtk-dark.css swap
# itself is broken for a plain GTK app) and instead follows the portal -- but this
# could not be told apart from "the mechanism does not work in this image" with the
# tools available. Shipped anyway because docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md's package() step
# already names this exact install path and it is a plain config file, not the kind
# of bespoke work the working brief's escalation rule would stop this change on --
# but its visual effect is UNVERIFIED, unlike the Kvantum and portal mechanisms.
[Settings]
gtk-theme-name=@NAME@
gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme=false
